\f1\fs22 The driver took his time, which was fine for Sarah; as the car wound its way among the eucalypts, she felt the memory of her first arrival at Sublime Point unwinding. She watched the bushfire-proof university-style office campus pass by without a word. Above, the metal-latticed minarets of Eloise\'92s impossible Middle-Eastern palace loomed; from the ground they performed none of their holographic disappearing tricks that Sarah saw from the air. As the car passed the hover-pad, the residence seemed to jump from back stage and model for Sarah, presenting its perspective-defying angles of smoked glass and metal alloy.\
