\f1\fs22 The car drove under the porte-coch\'e8re. Eloise was there waiting.\
Sarah stepped out of the car unassisted into dappled shade. The atmosphere tasted blue-green.\
\'93Sarah. I wasn\'92t expecting you.\'94 Eloise examined Sarah\'92s condition. \'93Are you on the way to the hospital? You know we have every comfort and facility for a home birth.\'94\
\'93We need to talk.\'94\
\'93We do.\'94 Eloise smiled. She led Sarah into the lobby, and through wide doors into an imposing lounge area designed more for reception than comfort.\
\'93Take a seat.\'94\
Sarah dropped into a couch, and realised she might need assistance getting out of it again.\
Eloise sat on the edge of a similar couch across from a coffee table that a jazz trio could use for a stage.\
Tea arrived, unaccompanied by milk, lemon, or sugar. Eloise poured. The maid transported it around to Sarah and receded through the furnishings.\
The room turned as expensively quiet as it was manicured.\
Eloise retrieved her device from her handbag and spoke into it. \'93Suppress surveillance.\'94 The device retired back to its resting place.\
\'93How are you feeling?\'94 Eloise sipped.\
Sarah tried to figure out how to reach her teacup without looking like a walrus with a middle ear infection. She fought with the cushions and pushed her way forward. The tea was in reach if she could compact Little Clinton\'92s lodgings down to the size of a bowling ball.\
\'93Johnny is derailing the project. He\'92s reckless.\'94\
\'93I\'92ve read the transcripts.\'94\
\'93He\'92s undermining my leadership.\'94\
\'93He went behind your back and acquired more\'85 kebabs.\'94 Eloise smiled when she used the project lingo.\
\'93After the apparatus exhibited unacceptable instabilities,\'94 Sarah stated.\
\'93Which the new washing machine has ironed out.\'94\
\'93We\'92re going too fast. The pentagram escalates the dangers.\'94\
\'93I am closer than I\'92ve ever been to harnessing Gyges energy.\'94\
\'93Closer than 
\f2\i you\'92ve
\f1\i0  ever been?\'94\
\'93Don\'92t toy with me,\'94 Eloise cautioned.\
\'93Your engineers are remarkably good at designing new washing machines.\'94\
\'93My engineers are the best in their field.\'94\
\'93At making weapons.\'94\
\'93Different objectives, same tech,\'94 Eloise waved the conversation away. \'93Sarah, let\'92s not pretend I don\'92t know what your bedtime reading has been recently.\'94\
Sarah put her cup down. \'93You researched kebabs before.\'94\
\'93Yes.\'94 \
\'93Fridge Force stopped you.\'94\
\'93They slowed me down.\'94\
Sarah chewed on that and retuned to her goal. \'93Johnny is reckless. He undermines Chip in front of everyone. He treats Quark like hired help. He ignores instructions. He thinks safety protocols are menu options.\'94\
\'93Johnny is operating within predefined tolerances.\'94\
\'93Not for me, he isn\'92t. Chip\'97\'94\
\'93A Fridge Force operative.\'94 Eloise sipped tea. \'93One that I have chosen to keep close.\'94\
\'93Are you saying he\'92s still\'97\'94\
\'93Spying for Fridge Force?\'94 Eloise pulled a face that skewed her mouth sideways.\
Sarah adjusted her posture for her bulk, and sat at an angle. \'93I can\'92t work with Johnny. Not anymore.\'94\
\'93The team is balanced exactly the way I want it.\'94\
\'93Then I must resign.\'94 Sarah held her breath.\
Eloise became as still as a portrait. \'93That would be unfortunate.\'94\
\'93I\'92ll divorce Alexander.\'94\
\'93He\'92ll forget you in weeks.\'94\
\'93Then what of your succession plan?\'94 Sarah heard the pitch of her voice rising.\
\'93None of this threatens my plan,\'94 Eloise said. \'93None of you\'85\'94 Eloise gestured to mean Sarah, her baby, and possibly Hayley and Kathy too. \'93\'85 threaten my plan.\'94\
Sarah sat straight and swallowed. \'93You know, this isn\'92t my first brush with a tyrant.\'94\
\'93I am aware,\'94 Eloise said quietly. \'93And I respect my elders.\'94\
That kicked Sarah harder than Little Clinton ever had.\
Eloise set her cup down.\
\'93You seem to be ignoring the progress we made,\'94 Eloise said. \'93We received a message from another universe.\'94\
\'93That\'92s one theory, and it doesn\'92t make Johnny useful.\'94\
\'93It makes the project useful.\'94\
\'93It asked about socks.\'94\
\'93Missing socks.\'94\
Sarah shrugged. \'93We have no idea what it means.\'94\
Eloise looked disappointed. \'93You\'92re better than that. Perhaps it\'92s baby brain. You really should be resting you know.\'94\
Sarah jutted her jaw defensively. \'93What am I missing?\'94\
\'93Things you wouldn\'92t miss if you weren\'92t having pissing matches with Johnny.\'94\
\'93Please don\'92t talk to a pregnant woman about bladder control.\'94\
Eloise laughed. \'93Quite right.\'94 She cackled as if recalling some long submerged memory. Then she returned to her thread. \'93The thing about the message? It was encrypted.\'94\
\'93I was there.\'94\
\'93Exactly the way we encrypt.\'94\
Sarah thought about that. \
\'93And somebody wanted to know where their missing socks had gone. Sarah, they wear\'85 socks. And they lose\'85 socks.\'94\
Sarah frowned. \'93They\'92re us.\'94\
\'93Or a version of us,\'94 Eloise said.\
Both women had forgotten their tea.\
Sarah sat back. Whatever had sent the message might have been shaped like a jellyfish or a municipal car park, but somewhere in its civilisation was a washing machine eating socks.\
\'93Sarah, why would I start firing people from the project that did that?\'94\
Sarah studied a na\'efve artwork so far across the room, she could have used opera glasses. \'93Fire Johnny.\'94\
\'93No.\'94\
\'93Then I resign.\'94\
\'93You already threatened that.\'94\
Sarah set her jaw. \'93I\'92m done with Kebab. I\'92m done with Shakti. I\'92ll go home.\'94\
\'93You are home.\'94\
\'93To my own apartment.\'94\
\'93I sold it.\'94\
Sarah stared. \'93You what?\'94\
Eloise shrugged. \'93The trappings of influence. Of which you, in this present moment, have very little.\'94\
Sarah tried to lift herself out of the couch. \'93Tax you.\'94\
\'93Sit down.\'94\
\'93I am sitting down.\'94 Sarah threw her hands up. \'93And I can\'92t get up.\'94 \
\'93Sarah.\'94\
\'93I\'92ll go stay with Tony.\'94\
Eloise laughed. Caught herself. Laughed again. \'93Sarah, do you know why you are here?\'94\
Sarah furrowed her brow. \'93To run Project Kebab.\'94\
\'93Hmmmm.\'94\
Sarah\'92s throat tightened.\
\'93Johnny is right.\'94\
\'93What?\'94\
\'93I\'92m putting you on leave.\'94\
\'93No, you\'92re not.\'94\
\'93Sarah, take a look at yourself. You need a forklift to get off a couch, for tax sake. And you could go into labour before this tea gets cold. What the tax are you trying to do to my grandson?\'94\
Sarah\'92s breath caught in her throat. She\'92d never heard Eloise raise her voice like that before. \
Eloise continued, calm again. \'93According to your supervisor\'97\'94\
\'93Who? Johnny?\'94\
Eloise reset. \'93According to your supervisor, you have been acting erratically in the workplace.\'94\
\'93I have been anything but erratic.\'94\
\'93You are pregnant.\'94\
\'93Those are not the same thing.\'94\
Eloise waved that away.\
\'93You can\'92t leave Johnny in charge.\'94\
\'93Oh Sarah, grow up.\'94\
\'93I 
\f2\i am 
\f1\i0 grown up.\'94\
Eloise checked herself and allowed a narrow, thin-lipped smile. \'93Yes, I keep forgetting that.\'94\
They sat quietly. Then Eloise said, \'93And you have committed industrial espionage against me.\'94\
\'93I was researching matters crucial to the performance of Project Kebab.\'94\
\'93You can\'92t afford the lawyers to make that case.\'94\
Eloise let the silence stretch. \'93You need rest. You will return home. To your townhouse. You are relieved from work duties. Your Project Kebab authorities are rescinded.\'94\
Sarah struggled to her feet. \'93Then I\'92m leaving. And in case there\'92s any misunderstanding, I\'92m taking my baby with me.\'94\
Outside, the driver was still waiting. He hurried around and opened the rear door. This time Sarah accepted the help getting in.\
\'93Where to?\'94 he asked.\
\'93Back to the city.\'94\
The driver looked at his console. His face changed.\
\'93Ma\'92am\'85\'94\
\'93Starborne One please, driver.\'94\
\'93I have other directions. I\'92m sorry.\'94\
The driver didn\'92t sound sorry.\
The car pulled away from Eloise\'92s House and turned south.\
The driver did not look at Sarah in the mirror.\

